## Final owner requirement before next corrective Work build — animation redesign + reboot skip bug
**Observed on real v0.6.1 FM-1:** after powering OFF then ON, the intro sometimes gets skipped automatically even though the user has not intentionally skipped it. Treat as P0 startup-state/input reliability defect. Also **replace the intro visual animation** with a new, original, clean, gracefully swirling cinematic design inspired in mood/motion by the **Sega Dreamcast boot animation** (no Sega logos or copied assets); retain the **separate original FM ambient PlayStation-1-inspired startup *sound*** from current issue. Maintain **8 seconds** maximum and persist/use selected Visualizer 1 or Polar Bloom, plus saved panel theme.

Source investigation `device/app.c::app_input_only()`: intro exits on `control || (k&~oldkeys) || intro_master_moved || now-intro_start>=10000u`. The `intro_master_moved` flag is set in `app_render()` whenever physical master ADC value differs from previous reading. Thus master ADC jitter/initialization drift may falsely skip intro even with no intentional control operation. This is a **plausible mechanism, not yet hardware-confirmed**. Inspect button/encoder/key startup state and order of UI/audio init too. Correct to skip only on a deliberate and debounced input edge *after initial stable baseline*, not on ordinary master ADC jitter; but an intentional knob/button/key gesture must still skip immediately, including an intentional volume control change if hardware can reliably distinguish it. Never interrupt recovery/safe-mode or play a surprise note; consume skip input.

Proposed original 8s choreography (static/deterministic bounded graphics, no expensive image shader):
1. near-dark screen, faint glowing particle/ripple;
2. luminous teal/orange/theme-aware ribbon draws a smooth spiral;
3. circle/ring develops into a water-crystal/sacred-geometry halo, with gentle perspective;
4. AQUORA wordmark/title materializes cleanly with soft FM swell;
5. visual transitions smoothly into the **saved selected visualizer** and its themed PLAY panel.
No use of Sega's exact boot animation, trademark swirl, logo or audio. Retain original synth design, not a Sony recording.

Important: 8-second intro is **not a forced boot delay**, no audible blast, respect physical master zero and optional startup sound mute. Audio onset must begin only after actual output ready and be clearly audible at normal volume. No residual graphics/audio CPU load after intro. Test real boot vs post-install first boot vs repeated complete power cycles, unpressed noisy controls, 8s timeout, every skip input, muted/master movement, saved visualizer/skin across restart. Link #16, #12, #15. Only claim hardware verified after owner tests.

**Status: added for next corrective release, not implemented.**
